  "script": "She booked the wrong hotel. A woman stormed to my desk demanding a suite from a reservation under her sister's name, at another property across town. I asked for photo ID that matched the booking. She had none, then called me incompetent loudly enough to empty the lobby chairs. She insisted I cancel someone else's reservation and give her the room because she was \u201calready here.\u201d My manager checked the security camera, heard the entire exchange, and asked her to show the confirmation email. The address at the top was not ours. Then the actual sister called, wondering why her reservation had been canceled online. The guest had done it herself while arguing with me. With the sister's room gone and our hotel nearly full, the woman finally booked our last standard room and paid the walk-in rate\u2014more than the suite she had tried to take. She read the address before signing this time.",
